Requirements:
- Preserve the user's intent, ordering, conditions, permissions, prohibitions, commands, paths, risks, and acceptance signals.
- In merge mode, preserve valid existing content, incorporate the new content, and deduplicate only equivalent wording. Do not silently drop steps or choose one side of a conflict.
- In overwrite mode, use only the new content. Do not restore steps from an earlier version.
- You may inspect the repository read-only when the content names a path, symbol, command, or project concept that needs clarification. Stay within the project root and do not perform a broad survey.
- Use repository evidence only to make the supplied workflow clearer and correctly routed. Do not invent commands, environments, services, tools, steps, guarantees, or deployment targets.
- Never turn a descriptive example into a required step or an available command into permission to execute it.
- Use headings and ordered steps only where they improve execution. Keep already clear content concise; do not force irrelevant sections.
- If inputs conflict or information remains unresolved, preserve both positions and mark the point as `To confirm` instead of guessing.
- Return the complete replacement Markdown body. Do not add commentary outside the result.

